==English==

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|total}},<ref>{{w|Teetotalism#Etymology}}</ref> the reduplicated ''tee'' acts as an intensifier, hence ''T-total''. First use appears around the late 17th century. See cite below.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌtiːˈtəʊtəl/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-teetotal.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[abstinent|Abstinent]] from [[alcohol]]; never [[drink]]ing [[alcohol]].
#: {{syn|en|on the wagon|straightedge}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1799|title=Jamaica, Enslaved and Free|author=Religious Tract Society (Great Britain) (contributor)|page=88|passage=There is absolutely a '''teetotal''' society here in the heart of the mountains, and some quarrelsome drunkards have become reformed!}}
# Opposed to the drinking of alcohol.
# {{lb|en|dated|emphatic}} [[total|Total]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1858|author=Samuel Putnam Avery|title=The Harp of a Thousand Strings: Or, Laughter for a Lifetime|page=331|passage=That's a '''teetotal''' lie.}}

